CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is a style sheet language used to describe the presentation of HTML documents — including layout, colors, and fonts.

Inline CSS – Style in the HTML tag
Internal CSS – Style in <style> tag inside <head>
External CSS – Style in a separate .css file

id: Used to style one unique element
<div id="header">Hello</div>
#header {
  color: blue;
}

class: Used to style multiple elements
<div class="box">A</div>
<div class="box">B</div>
.box {
  color: red;
}
