How to make a website responsive using CSS?

• Use media queries
• Use percentages/flexbox
• Avoid fixed units

-> Media Queries (Core of Responsiveness)
Apply styles based on screen size
/* For tablets */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  body {
    background-color: lightblue;
  }
}

/* For mobile */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .container {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}

-> Use the Viewport Meta Tag
This tells the browser how to scale your page on different devices
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

-> Use Flexible Layouts (Avoid Fixed Widths)
Instead of fixed sizes like px, use flexible units:
% (percentage)
vw, vh (viewport width/height)
em, rem

-> Use Flexbox or Grid
Modern layout systems make responsiveness easier
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
